## Failed actions (an error toast) and the panic overlay

error-details = Details
error-generic = That didn't work. Try again; if it keeps failing, copy the details for your admin.
area-load-failed = This part of the app could not be loaded. Check your connection, then try again. If it still fails, reload the app: a new version may have come out.
area-reload = Reload app
error-network = The server can't be reached. Check your connection and try again.
error-notification-not-allowed = Notifications are blocked for this app. Allow them in your browser's or system's settings, then try again.
error-notification-unsupported = This browser can't show notifications.
error-notification-refused = The system didn't show the notification. Check its notification settings, such as focus or do-not-disturb modes.
error-captive-portal = This network wants you to sign in first. Open a web page to sign in, then try again.
error-untrusted-certificate = The server's certificate isn't trusted. On a network that inspects encrypted traffic, use another network or ask your IT to install the company certificate on this device; if it happens everywhere, the server's certificate may be broken: tell your administrator.
error-not-space-member = This person isn't in the space yet. Invite them to the space first, then add them to the channel.
error-forbidden = You don't have permission for this. Ask an admin of the space or workspace.
error-signed-out = Your sign-in has expired. Sign in again, then try once more.
error-rate-limited = Too many requests at once. Wait a moment and try again.
error-too-large = That is too large for the server. Try something smaller.
error-server-trouble = The server has a problem right now. Try again in a few minutes.
error-conflict = Someone changed this at the same time. Look at the current state and try again.
error-not-found = This doesn't exist any more. It may have been deleted or moved.
error-call-microphone-denied = The browser blocked the microphone. Allow it for this site (the icon in the address bar), then join again.
error-call-microphone-missing = No microphone was found. Connect one, then join again.
error-call-microphone-in-use = The microphone can't be opened. Close other apps that use it and try again.
error-call-camera-denied = The browser blocked the camera. Allow it for this site (the icon in the address bar), then turn the camera on again.
error-call-camera-missing = No camera was found. Connect one, then turn the camera on again.
error-call-camera-in-use = The camera can't be opened. Close other apps that use it and try again.
error-call-camera-unsupported = This camera's picture format isn't supported, so your video stays off. Try another camera.
error-call-screen-unavailable = Your screen can't be shared from here.
error-call-unsupported = This browser can't make calls. Use a current Chrome, Edge, Firefox or Safari, or the TeamCraft app.
error-call-server-unreachable = The call server can't be reached. The network may block calls (UDP); try another network or ask your admin.
error-call-background-required = Your organization requires a background behind your camera, which the browser can't add yet. Turn your camera on in the TeamCraft app.
error-call-encryption-pending = This device can't join the call yet: it is still being let into the conversation's encryption. Keep TeamCraft open on another of your devices, or wait for a member to come online, then join again. For a meeting, its organizer may have to open it once first.
error-call-move-refused = The call wasn't moved: the meeting room doesn't match what was announced in the conversation. Stay in this call, or join the meeting room from the list if you trust it.
error-call-speakers-unavailable = The chosen speakers can't be used here. The test sound played on the default output.
error-call-speakers-missing = No speakers were found. Connect speakers or headphones and try again.
error-call-sound-blocked = The browser didn't let the page play sound. Click anywhere on the page, then try again.
action-running = Working…
panic-title = Something went wrong
panic-body = The app ran into an error and has to be reloaded. What you were typing just now may be lost.
panic-reload = Reload
panic-details-label = Technical details for your admin (version and where the error happened)

